# Frontend Localization Rules

## Core Rule: NO HARDCODED TEXT IN FRONTEND COMPONENTS

### ✅ REQUIRED: Use Lingui Translation Macro
```tsx
import { t } from "@lingui/macro";

// All user-facing text MUST use the t macro
<h1>{t`Welcome to Job Applications`}</h1>
<button>{t`Submit Application`}</button>
<Input placeholder={t`Enter your email address`} />
<SelectValue placeholder={t`Select an option`} />
```

### ❌ FORBIDDEN: Hardcoded Text Strings
```tsx
// NEVER hardcode user-facing text
<h1>Welcome to Job Applications</h1>  // ❌ WRONG
<button>Submit Application</button>   // ❌ WRONG
<Input placeholder="Enter your email" />  // ❌ WRONG
<SelectValue placeholder="Select option" />  // ❌ WRONG
```

## What Must Be Localized

### 1. All User-Facing Text
- Button labels, form labels, placeholders
- Error messages, success messages
- Page titles, headings, navigation items
- Tooltips, help text, status labels
- Loading messages, count displays

### 2. Dynamic Content
- Pluralization: `{count} {count === 1 ? t`item` : t`items`}`
- Conditional text: `{isActive ? t`Active` : t`Inactive`}`
- Dynamic placeholders: `placeholder={t`Search by ${searchType}...`}`

### 3. Implementation Requirements
- Every component displaying text MUST import: `import { t } from "@lingui/macro";`
- After adding new strings, run: `pnpm run messages:extract && pnpm exec lingui compile`
- Test with different locales to ensure proper display

## Exceptions (Technical Identifiers Only)
- Font names: `"Arial", "Cambria", "Garamond"`
- Brand names: `"LinkedIn", "GitHub", "YouTube"`
- URLs and paths: `"/dashboard/settings"`
- Technical values: `value="en-US"`
- Code comments and console logs

## Code Review Checklist
- [ ] All user-facing text uses `t` macro
- [ ] No hardcoded strings in JSX
- [ ] Import statement includes `t` from `@lingui/macro`
- [ ] Dynamic content handles pluralization correctly
- [ ] Translation extraction run after changes
- [ ] Component documented in `docs/10-architecture/Frontend-Components.md`

## Documentation Requirements

### CRITICAL: All Frontend Components Must Be Documented

When adding or modifying frontend components:

1. **Update Frontend Components Map**: Add/update entry in `docs/10-architecture/Frontend-Components.md`
   - Include component path
   - Mark localization status (✅ Fully localized, ⚠️ Partially localized, ❌ Not localized)
   - Note any special localization considerations (e.g., constant arrays, dynamic content)

2. **Verify Complete Localization**:
   ```bash
   # Search for hardcoded strings in your component
   grep -n "placeholder=\"[^{]" your-component.tsx
   grep -n "alt=\"[^{]" your-component.tsx
   grep -n "title=\"[^{]" your-component.tsx
   
   # Run translation extraction
   pnpm run messages:extract
   pnpm exec lingui compile
   ```

3. **Update Documentation After Changes**:
   - If you add new components, add them to Frontend-Components.md
   - If you fix localization issues, update the status in Frontend-Components.md
   - Keep the documentation synchronized with code changes

### Documentation Structure
- **Location**: `docs/10-architecture/Frontend-Components.md`
- **Cross-references**: Linked from `docs/10-architecture/Modules.md` and `docs/maps/README.md`
- **Purpose**: Maintain a complete catalog of all frontend components for future reference

## Enforcement
- ESLint rule: `@lingui/no-unlocalized-strings`
- Pre-commit hooks run translation extraction
- CI pipeline validates translation integrity
- **Documentation review**: Verify Frontend-Components.md is updated

